An updated version of the Hearse Windows client is now available from 
http://hearse.krollmark.com.  This is not a required upgrade, all 
previous versions of the client will continue to work fine.

The only major change in this release is a simplification of the Hearse 
protocol.  In my tests, this increased upload speed by ~25%.

Two new command line options:

/c - uses the old protocol (just included in case anyone has problems 
with the new one)

/r - resets the 'last uploaded' timestamp (that is, prevents Hearse 
attempting to upload old bones files).  Included as a workaround for 
users who sometimes run into problems with this.

Please let me know if you run into any problems with this release, or 
have any suggestions for improvements.

